      "headline": "Put Down the Heavy Rock",
      "keyInsight": "Seekers love asking complicated questions about past lives, subtle heavens, and mystical cosmic planes. But asking complex philosophy while your heart burns with daily jealousy and worry is like asking about the chemical formula of smoke while your house is burning down. Freedom is not an encyclopedia of secret knowledge. It is the simple, practical act of opening your fingers and dropping the heavy stone you have carried up the hill for years.",
      "content": "A student once walked up to the master carrying an enormous load of anxiety. He asked long, tangled questions about the ultimate nature of existence and how to attain supreme perfection. The master smiled, pointed to a large boulder resting by the roadside, and asked, Is that rock heavy? The student replied, Yes, of course it is! The master chuckled and said, Not if you don't pick it up. All your daily stress comes from grabbing things that do not belong to you and wondering why your arms ache.\n\nPeople often ask how to balance deep meditation with jobs, family duties, and bustling city noise. They worry they need to abandon their normal lives and retreat into a silent cave forever. But you do not need to quit your job to practice letting go. When you wash a dish, wash the dish completely without mentally fighting the grease. When someone insults you, hear the sound vibrating in the air, and let it vanish into space without grabbing it and gluing it onto your forehead.\n\nThe real secret of enlightenment is that there is nothing extra to buy, build, or conquer. It is purely subtractive. You let go of wanting pleasant things to last forever, and you let go of wanting unpleasant things to disappear right now. In the middle of that letting go, your heart becomes like a still pool in a deep forest. Clear, unmoving, and reflecting the sky without holding a single cloud.",
